---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SUPPORT_EMAIL, POLICY_UPDATED } from "../config";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy | Our Expenses"
  description="Our Expenses stores everything on your iPhone and sends nothing anywhere."
>
  <div class="shell prose">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="eyebrow">Last updated {POLICY_UPDATED}</p>

    <p>
      Our Expenses runs on your iPhone and talks to nothing.
    </p>

    <h2>What the app stores</h2>
    <p>
      Three things are stored in your device's local storage: the people you add with
      their monthly incomes, the expenses you save, and the split each saved
      expense produced.
    </p>

    <h2>What leaves your device</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing. There is no account, no login, no server, no analytics, no
      advertising and no third-party kit reporting on you. The app makes no
      network request of its own.
    </p>

    <h2>What Apple sees</h2>
    <p>
      Apple runs the download under its own privacy policy. If you switched on
      "Share With App Developers" in your iOS settings, Apple may pass me crash
      reports and usage counts, aggregated and stripped of anything naming you. I
      never see who you are, who you split with, or what you spent.
    </p>

    <h2>Backups</h2>
    <p>
      Backing your iPhone up to iCloud or to a computer includes this app's data
      along with the rest of the phone. Apple's encryption and policies govern
      the backup from there.
    </p>

    <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
    <p>
      Remove a person from the People screen. Delete one expense, a selection, or
      the whole history from the History screen. Deleting the app takes
      everything it stored with it.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>The app collects nothing from anyone, at any age.</p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      A new version replaces this page and carries a new date at the top. The app
      stays offline whatever this page says.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions go to <a href={"mailto:" + SUPPORT_EMAIL}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
